    "turn_idx": 104,
    "turn_text": "One of the other things that you were involved in over the last couple of weeks, all the attention on the Obamacare repeal effort, tended to be on the Senate. dealing with things behind the scenes in ways, calling governors exerting pressure on people. There's a story of when Obamacare was passing initially, Joe Donnelly, when he was in the house that you got Father Hasberg from Notre Dame to call him and do some pressure. Wait, did you ever hear that? Oh, that was public back then.",
