  {
    "episode_id": 70873,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70873.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 108,
    "turn_text": "The Affordable Care Act is something that is a major accomplishment of 20 million people having access to affordable quality health care. Much more needs to be done, of course. But I'm very proud of that. And one of the reasons I stayed in Congress when we didn't win the White House and the Senate was to protect the Affordable Care Act because I knew it would come under siege. What's important about our success with it for the year? I mean, we started four days after the",
