    "turn_text": "you seen here? Well, this is an institution that has been built on over 200 years of pecking order. One, I'll be for you, you'll be for me, I'll be for you, and I go up the line. When I ran, it was like, well, wait a minute, it's not your turn. No, you've had over 200 years. It is our turn. And that's the way it is. And people even said, who said she could run? But Joni lit my engine further to run. But I had a lot of support and I felt pretty confident about winning. I also wouldn't have asked people to go out on the limb. They're both for me. So I haven't been so much a victim or I didn't even cared. In other words, that's your problem. It's not mine. But I do believe that it has to be factored in when we're encouraging women to run. that there is an element that is there, perhaps it's generational, and it will go away. And let's",
