    "turn_text": "I think, no, I think, listen, whatever he said since then is, know where somebody said before. I mean, during the campaign and the rest about immigrants, about women, you know. So this is about a person who is the president of the United States. If we can find common ground, then we will. That everything is its own discussion. It doesn't anoint anybody in any way. It just says we were able to come to terms on something. As I said before, we worked very closely with George W. Bush. I love the Bush family. You know that all of them. What could be worse than the war in Iraq? They took us into war in Iraq, and yet we could find common ground as objectionable, shall we say, of some of the comments that the president has made, and they are objectionable, especially if he really believes that nothing can be worse than the war in Iraq.",
