    "turn_text": "how do you do that? Here's the thing. You've laid out three scenarios, how we work together, how we don't, and how we are proactively negative. Many of the people who are anti-Trump certainly want to protect the dreamers. They want to protect the dreamers. So as you weigh the equities in these things, you have a chance to do it. had the agreement on lifting the debt ceiling, that's the less immediate in people's lives, but they saw that he came our way. And that was important. It wasn't a compromise, it was he came our way. And we want to stop some of the bad things that they put forward. And that list is so long that we could just spend a day on it for sure, just listing. But that takes us to your third point. in terms of the election. Elections about differentiating. It's about what we stand for more positively. Our better deal, better jobs, better pay, better. a better future and people want to see what that is. And it also involves a differentiation. This is how we are different from them. And that's a legitimate difference on policy. This isn't personal. It's about",
