    "turn_text": "all, one of the things we did was build our, and I consider that part of my legacy, to build the grassroots part of our fundraising. The fact is that I do have a following across the country that is very progressive or moderate but not pragmatic. They're not about any special interest. And so there's no, when people talk about money in politics, which I do all the time, that it must be reduced, we're not talking about any special interest money coming to the House Democrats. I think that it may be you're talking about 2% of what comes to the DCCC coming from a pragmatic money that gives both the Republicans and the Democrats. So it's not that. But the fact is, is that we try to take it to a place where it is idealistic support for the Democrats. They believe in what we believe in, A, and B, that helps us grow the grassroots. And that only happens. The grassroots funding is not automatic. They want to see a fight. They want to see us fighting for them. I don't mean to fight per se, but a fight for them when they see their interest under assault. And so it's not just, oh, I'm a Democrat. I'm going to send in my $10 every month. Show",
